<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 224)</h2>
<p><b>Session minutes are now attributed.</b> Not by guessing — by architecture.</p>
<ul>
<li>In a shared review, <b>Record the Session</b> invites every participant's Asobi to record its own microphone (each person consents, and sees the same red badge). Every voice transcribes on the machine it was spoken at, under its own name — <b>only the text</b> comes back. Audio never leaves anyone's machine.</li>
<li>The merged minutes read <code>Sarah: the logo feels small</code> — in order, against the shot that was on screen.</li>
<li><b>No headphones? Handled.</b> Your mic also hears the call through your speakers — but your own voice reaches your mic instantly, while everyone else's copy crossed the network first. The late duplicate is recognised and discarded. Physics does the attribution.</li>
<li>The timeline stays fully yours to drive while recording — capture listens, it never steers.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Everyone updates together:</b> shared reviews need all participants on this build (sync protocol 4).</p>
]]></description>
